  "question": {
    "text": "A particle is travelling along a straight line $O X$. The distance $x$ (in metre) of the particle from 0 at a time t is given by $x=37+27 t-t^{3}$, where t is time in seconds. The distance of the particle from $O$ when it comes to rest is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "jT4PE",
      "text": "$81 \\mathrm{m}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "03Sts",
      "text": "$91 \\mathrm{m}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "67Gzo",
      "text": "$101 \\mathrm{m}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "AJg6I",
      "text": "$111 \\mathrm{m}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given, $x=37+27 t-t^{3}$\r\n$$\r\nv=\\frac{d x}{d t}=27-3 t^{2}\r\n$$\r\nAccording to problem,\r\n$$\r\nv=0 \\Rightarrow 27-3 t^{2}=0\r\n$$\r\nHere, $t=3 \\mathrm{s}$\r\n$$\r\nx=37+27 \\times 3-(3)^{2}=91 \\mathrm{m}\r\n$$",
    "image": null
